<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Johor Bahru</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tanjung Puteri</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johor">Johor</a> Bahru is the capital of the Malaysian state of Johor, at the southern tip of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malay-peninsula">Malay Peninsula</a> across the strait from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/singapore">Singapore</a>. Founded in 1855 as Tanjung Puteri by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/temenggong-daeng-ibrahim">Temenggong Daeng Ibrahim</a>, it was renamed and made the capital by his son Abu Bakar in the 1860s. A causeway opened in 1924 links it to Singapore.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/johor-bahru.jpg" alt="Johor Bahru" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: R&amp;F Malaysia · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E5%AF%8C%E5%8A%9B%E5%85%AC%E4%B8%BB%E6%B9%BE_R%26F_Princess_Cove_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
